 # Detector migration
+
+## Source continuity metadata — proposed isolated patch
+
+`Frame` and `Observation` gain an optional trailing `capture` field; existing positional constructors remain valid. Live streams create a new opaque epoch on camera reopen or native geometry change and preserve it through resizing and inference. The optional identity adapter clears only the affected camera's temporal and sampling state, ignores duplicate/out-of-order evidence, and requires fresh agreement after discontinuities. Snapshot mode preserves the same metadata. JSON configuration, archive files and live-preview files remain unchanged. This patch alone does not invalidate an old browser overlay immediately at disconnection; source-epoch status and live confirmation are separate work.
 
 The rebuild covers the Python detector, its schemas, tests, and distributions. The Python rewrite preserved the web archive contract. The subsequent application setup work adds a combined web/native download and optional parent-controlled shutdown.
 
